  hero_eyebrow:"Bitcoin risk model · open",
  hero_h1:"Know when Bitcoin is <em>cheap</em> — and act on it.",
  hero_lead:"A risk metric compresses price, trend and on-chain valuation into a single number from 0 to 1. Low = historically cheap; high = historically stretched.",
  hero_p2:"Dynamic DCA uses that number to decide how much to buy: more when risk is low, nothing when it's high — instead of buying the same amount blindly.",
  hero_p3:"<b>Why does it beat plain DCA?</b> Conventional DCA buys a fixed sum on a fixed day, ignoring whether Bitcoin is cheap or expensive. Dynamic DCA puts the same total money to work mostly at low-risk moments, which historically accumulated far more Bitcoin per dollar.",
