  bs_disc_eye:"This is not financial advice",
  bs_disc_p:"An educational tool only. The risk metric is a transparent, replicable composite built from public price and on-chain data \u2014 not the official metric of any third party. Past performance and historical simulations do not predict future results. Crypto is extremely volatile and you can lose all of your capital. These strategies involve opportunity cost (sitting in cash during rallies) and sequence-of-returns risk; taxes, fees and slippage are ignored in the examples. Always do your own research, never invest more than you can afford to lose, and consult a licensed advisor if unsure.",
  ctr_eye:"Contribute to this project", ctr_h:"Keep the signal open and free",
  ctr_p1:"This model has no paywall and no token to shill. It will never be a pay-to-use site: no subscription fees, no \u201CPremium\u201D account, nothing locked behind a tier. Every update and improvement we make stays free and available to everyone \u2014 because open, auditable tools are how we keep knowledge in everyone's hands, owned by no one and impossible to quietly switch off.",
  ctr_p2:"Donating in Bitcoin is part of the point. Every sat sent peer-to-peer is a small step out of a fiat system built on permission and dilution, and toward money no one can print away. If this saved you a bad buy \u2014 or taught you something \u2014 consider chipping in. Pooling our efforts is how independent work survives.",
