  math_p2:"with a ≈ 8.49×10⁻¹⁶, b ≈ 5.2912, T ≈ 1461 days (halving cycle), A₀ ≈ 0.68, κ ≈ 0.45, t_ref ≈ 5500. The exponential form guarantees positivity and turns the oscillation into an additive term in log space.",
  math_h2:"2 · Instantaneous drift",
  math_p3:"The expected return (drift) is obtained by differentiating the log of the model; it anchors the stochastic layer:",
